  "raw_text": "the bun texture? User: I would say the right amount of sauce. Too much is too sloppy and too little is not enough. So you need the right amount of sauce and a nice fresh bun with the sesame seeds. Agent: That makes perfect sense. The sauce balance and bun freshness are definitely key. On the flip side, what are the top two or three things that would make a Big Mac \"bad\" for you? For instance, if it were soggy, dry, cold, under-salted, too greasy, or stale? User: I would say if they forgot to put the cheese on it and it didn't have cheese and if it was way too saucy and messy. Agent: Missing the cheese and being too saucy would definitely be disappointing. If a Big Mac was unavailable, what would you order instead, including the chain and the specific item? User: I would probably go to Burger King and get a Whopper. Agent: Okay, a Whopper from Burger King. Why do you consider that the closest replacement for a Big Mac? User: It's kind of like the Big Mac sister, it's the competitor b",
